      <section class="editorial-chapter">
        <h2>Departmental Analysis: Teachers, Police &amp; Administrative Cadres</h2>
        <p>
          Specific departmental groupings command substantial budgetary allocations in the Karnataka state accounts:
        </p>

        <div class="cadre-card-grid">
          <div class="cadre-box education">
            <h4>School Education: PST &amp; GPT Teachers</h4>
            <div class="cadre-badge">Department of School Education &amp; Literacy</div>
            <p><strong>Covered Ranks:</strong> Primary School Teachers (Scale 8: ₹37,900), Graduate Primary Teachers (Scale 10: ₹43,100), and Secondary High School Teachers.</p>
            <p><strong>Impact:</strong> Teachers represent the largest single workforce cohort in the state. Under the 8th CPC, entry basic pay for GPT teachers will climb to <strong>₹98,268 per month</strong> under the 2.28 factor, significantly elevating living standards.</p>
            <span class="cadre-footer">GPT Teacher (7th PC): ₹43,100 | 8th CPC (2.28x): <strong>₹98,268</strong></span>
          </div>

          <div class="cadre-box police">
            <h4>Karnataka State Police (KSP)</h4>
            <div class="cadre-badge">Law Enforcement, KSRP &amp; City Police</div>
            <p><strong>Covered Ranks:</strong> Constables (Scale 4: ₹30,350), Head Constables (Scale 8: ₹37,900), Sub-Inspectors (Scale 11: ₹47,650), and Police Inspectors (Scale 14: ₹58,250).</p>
            <p><strong>Impact:</strong> Police personnel draw specialized uniform, conveyance, and risk allowances. Confirmed constables will see their baseline basic pay jump to <strong>₹69,198 per month</strong>.</p>
