      </section>

      <section class="editorial-chapter">
        <h2>House Rent Allowance (HRA) Classification Across Karnataka</h2>
        <p>
          In Karnataka, House Rent Allowance is categorized into <strong>four distinct geographic groups</strong> under state finance rules:
        </p>

        <div class="city-classification-grid">
          <div class="city-box tier-groupA">
            <h4>Group A (Bengaluru Metropolitan Area)</h4>
            <div class="badge-tag">Bruhat Bengaluru Mahanagara Palike (BBMP)</div>
            <p><strong>Projected HRA Rate:</strong> 27% of Basic Pay (or enhanced central metro ceiling).</p>
            <p><strong>Covered Areas:</strong> Bengaluru Urban District, BBMP limits, and contiguous urban development clusters.</p>
            <span class="card-footer-note">Reflects the highest commercial and residential rental cost tier in the state.</span>
          </div>

          <div class="city-box tier-groupB">
            <h4>Group B (Major Municipal Corporations)</h4>
            <div class="badge-tag">Population 5 Lakh to 50 Lakh</div>
